From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:42:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Score the E/M primary diagnosis, and ignore dots in E/M
 diagnoses

E/M diagnoses were scored as an order-blind set, so a coder who buried
the right primary at the bottom of the list lost nothing. The primary
now carries half the Dx weight, all or nothing, earned only when listed
first (the IP/OP PDx rule); the secondaries share the other half
wherever listed. Applies to E/M and ED Profee. Stored scores are left
as graded; the review says when a result predates the rule.

Also: the coder's Dx box says 'dot optional', but E/M compared codes
with dots, so E119 against a key of E11.9 scored as wrong. Dots are now
ignored on both sides, as IP/OP grading already does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
